# {{.AppName}} — agent guide

This app was scaffolded by **gor** (Go on Rails): a Go API (Echo + pgx +
sqlc + goose) with a React + Vite + TypeScript SPA (TanStack Query, React
Hook Form + Zod, Tailwind v4 + shadcn/ui), shipped as one binary.

## Golden rule

**Prefer gor generators over hand-writing boilerplate.** They produce both
the backend and the matching frontend, wired together, and track what they
generated in `.gor/manifest.json` so later schema changes regenerate
everything consistently.

```bash
gor g resource post title:string body:text published:bool   # full-stack CRUD
gor g model tag name:string                                 # data layer only (no API/frontend)
gor g migration add_slug_to_posts slug:string               # schema change + auto-regen
gor g sync post --live                                      # toggle flags on existing resource
gor g auth            # sessions, roles, guards, login UI
gor g auth-emails     # password reset + email verification
gor g jobs && gor g job send_welcome_email [--every 1h|--cron "0 9 * * *"] [--live]
gor g realtime        # SSE + Postgres NOTIFY, React hooks
gor g mailer welcome  # SMTP email + Mailpit dev catcher
gor g uploads         # file storage + upload control (field type: file)
gor g observability   # error reports (SENTRY_DSN) + Prometheus /metrics
```

Field types: `string text int bigint bool decimal timestamp uuid references file`.
Resource flags: `--protected` (needs auth), `--live` (needs realtime),
`--headless` (schema/hooks/Form building blocks, no pages/routes),
`--service`, `--api-only`, `--force`. Per-app flag defaults can live in
`.gor/config.json` (`{ "resource": { "headless": true } }`); explicit flags win.

## Rules

- **Never remove `gor:` marker comments** (`// gor:imports`, `// gor:routes`,
  `{/* gor:routes */}`, `{/* gor:protected-routes */}`, `{/* gor:nav */}`,
  `// gor:workers`, `// gor:periodic`, `# gor:services`) — generators insert there.
- **Never edit `internal/db/gen/`** — sqlc output. Change `queries/*.sql` or
  migrations instead, then run `gor db gen` (or let `gor dev` do it on save).
- Schema changes go through `gor g migration` + `gor db migrate` — don't edit
  applied migration files.
- Hand-edited generated files are safe: sync skips them and lists what to
  update manually.
- Config is env-only: add new vars to `.env.example` (and `.env`), read them
  in `internal/config` or via `os.Getenv`.

## Everyday commands

```bash
gor dev          # API + Vite (+ worker if present), hot reload
gor db setup     # Docker Postgres + migrate   (reset wipes; seed runs cmd/seed)
gor build        # production binary (bin/{{.AppName}}); --image for Docker
```

## Verify your changes

```bash
go test ./...                 # backend tests
(cd web && npx tsc -b)        # strict typecheck of the frontend
go build ./...                # compile check
```

## Layout

Feature-based: one Go package per resource under `internal/<name>/`, one
React folder under `web/src/features/<plural>/`, typed clients in
`web/src/api/`. Shared pieces: `internal/httpx` (errors/validation),
`internal/auth` (guards: `auth.Require`, `auth.RequireRole`),
`internal/jobs` (`jobs.Enqueue`), `internal/realtime`
(`realtime.Publish`), `internal/mailer`, `internal/storage`.
